Implement Upgrade-30 as a bounded production-fleet safety slice for cvsz/zcoder.

Objective: add a PostgreSQL session advisory run lease for distributed continuous-engineering mutual exclusion without exposing the PostgreSQL backend before stale-writer fencing exists.

Requirements:
- define a minimal generic RunLease protocol while preserving the existing filesystem UpgradeRunLease;
- derive a deterministic signed BIGINT advisory-lock key from a non-empty namespace;
- hold one PostgreSQL connection/session from acquire through release;
- acquire with pg_try_advisory_lock and release with pg_advisory_unlock on the same session;
- fail closed on contention, query errors, lost ownership, or connection return failures;
- ensure contention immediately returns the checked-out connection;
- add unit tests for lifecycle/error paths and a live DATABASE_URL integration test for cross-session exclusion/release;
- document that advisory locking alone is exclusivity, not stale-writer fencing;
- do not expose PostgreSQL as a ContinuousEngineeringPipeline/CLI backend until fence-aware ledger mutations are implemented;
- preserve Upgrade-20 execution authority, Upgrade-24 budgets, JSON/SQLite behavior, local-only push default, and all existing CI/security gates.
